Functional Requirement Document (FRD)
Flight Booking Application
1. Introduction
Purpose: Define functional requirements and system behavior.
Scope: Flight search, booking, payment, user and admin management.
2. Stakeholders
End Users – Customers booking flights
Admin Users – Manage system
Payment Gateway – External provider
Airline Systems – Flight data providers
3. User Roles
Guest User – Search flights
Registered User – Book/manage bookings
Admin – Manage system
4. Functional Modules
Flight Search
Flight Selection
Booking & Reservation
Payment Processing
Booking Management
User Management
Notifications
Admin Module
5. Flight Search Module
Search by origin, destination, date
One-way, round-trip, multi-city
Display flight details
Filter and sort results
6. Flight Selection Module
Select flight
View fare details
Select seat class
Select seats
7. Booking Module
Enter passenger details
Validate information
Add multiple passengers
Generate booking summary
Confirm booking
8. Payment Module
Select payment method
Redirect to gateway
Process success/failure
Confirm booking on success
9. Booking Management
View bookings
Cancel bookings
Modify bookings
Trigger refunds
10. User Management
Register user
Login/logout
Update profile
Reset password
View booking history
11. Notifications
Booking confirmation
Payment confirmation
Cancellation notification
Flight reminders
12. Admin Module
Manage flights
View bookings
Manage users
Generate reports
Manage pricing
13. Process Flow
Search → Select → Enter Details → Payment → Confirmation
14. Business Rules
Valid passenger details required
Payment required for booking
Cancellation per airline policy
Dynamic seat availability
15. Data Requirements
User Data
Flight Data
Booking Data
Payment Data
16. External Interfaces
Airline APIs
Payment Gateway
Notification Services
17. Assumptions
Accurate airline data
Payment system availability
Valid user inputs
18. Acceptance Criteria
Users can search and book flights
Bookings confirmed after payment
Users can manage bookings
Notifications sent for events
